{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>My unformed substance</b> — this is the first body, which was like a small drop, and it is from the root of ויגלום, and like it: וחילופיהן בגולם שאין לו לב רק גוף לבדו (their substitutes [are regarded] as a golem that has no mind but body alone)." "And the meaning of <b>and in Your book</b> — all of them, [i.e.,] his limbs, as though his form were written in a book, and it emerges without addition and without diminution." "<b>Days were fashioned</b> — like in the meaning of הרים יולדו, from the root יצירה." "And the meaning of <b>and not one of them</b> — by way of alef, for in Your book all my limbs and their arrangement were written in those days when they were fashioned, and not one of them was distinguished and separate — for in the power of generation the form of the eye and the ear and the heart is in the first drop, even though no separate limb is there."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {0 "The reference after 'וכמוהו' appears to be to a rabbinic dictum about a golem; left in Hebrew as it functions as a cited parallel."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:17.114967836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}